---
import NeuronModels from './NeuronModels.astro';
---

<section class="model-architecture" aria-labelledby="architecture-title">
  <p class="section-label">Architecture</p>
  <div>
    <h2 id="architecture-title">How the model generates SPW-Rs</h2>
    <p class="architecture-copy">
      The prefrontal cortex (PFC) drives both CA3 and CA1. In the simplified network,
      cortical input reaches CA3 directly through a mossy fiber-like pathway that bypasses
      the dentate gyrus, while a temporoammonic pathway provides input to CA1. CA3 then
      drives CA1 through the Schaffer collaterals. Together, these cortical inputs help
      determine when ripple events emerge across slow-oscillation states.
    </p>
    <p class="architecture-copy">
      Within CA3, recurrent excitation among pyramidal neurons generates large population
      events that propagate to CA1. In CA1, recurrent inhibition between interneurons helps
      organize the incoming excitation into synchronized sharp-wave ripple activity. The diagrams
      highlight the model's distinct connectivity: pyramidal–pyramidal connections in CA3 are absent
      in CA1, while interneuron–interneuron connections in CA1 are absent in CA3.
    </p>
    <div class="architecture-panel" role="group" aria-label="Network connectivity and neuron models">
      <svg class="region-diagram" viewBox="0 0 560 300" role="img" aria-labelledby="region-diagram-title region-diagram-desc">
        <title id="region-diagram-title">PFC input to CA3 and CA1, with a CA3 projection to CA1</title>
        <desc id="region-diagram-desc">PFC projects directly to CA3 through a mossy fiber-like model pathway that bypasses DG, and to CA1 through the temporoammonic pathway. Schaffer collaterals carry activity from CA3 to CA1.</desc>
        <defs>
          <marker id="architecture-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="10" refY="5" markerWidth="9" markerHeight="9" markerUnits="userSpaceOnUse" orient="auto">
            <path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" class="arrowhead" />
          </marker>
        </defs>
        <path class="connection" d="M 256 77 L 123 213" marker-end="url(#architecture-arrow)" />
        <path class="connection" d="M 304 77 L 437 213" marker-end="url(#architecture-arrow)" />
        <path class="connection" d="M 136 240 L 424 240" marker-end="url(#architecture-arrow)" />
        <circle class="region" cx="280" cy="52" r="34" />
        <circle class="region" cx="100" cy="240" r="34" />
        <circle class="region" cx="460" cy="240" r="34" />
        <text class="region-name" x="280" y="58">PFC</text>
        <text class="region-name" x="100" y="246">CA3</text>
        <text class="region-name" x="460" y="246">CA1</text>
        <text x="96" y="116">Mossy fiber-like input</text>
        <text class="diagram-note" x="96" y="138">DG bypassed in the model</text>
        <text x="456" y="116">Temporoammonic</text>
        <text x="456" y="138">pathway</text>
        <text x="280" y="222">Schaffer collaterals</text>
      </svg>
      <div class="local-circuits">
        <div class="local-circuit">
          <h3>CA3 · Recurrent excitation</h3>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 260 140" role="img" aria-labelledby="ca3-circuit-title">
            <title id="ca3-circuit-title">Two pyramidal neurons with reciprocal excitatory connections and a PV interneuron</title>
            <defs>
              <marker id="ca3-excitatory-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="10" refY="5" markerWidth="9" markerHeight="9" markerUnits="userSpaceOnUse" orient="auto">
                <path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" class="arrowhead" />
              </marker>
              <marker id="ca3-inhibitory-bar" viewBox="0 0 4 14" refX="2" refY="7" markerWidth="4" markerHeight="14" markerUnits="userSpaceOnUse" orient="auto">
                <rect x="0.75" y="1" width="2.5" height="12" class="inhibitory-head" />
              </marker>
            </defs>
            <path class="connection supporting" d="M 73 95 L 114 46" marker-end="url(#ca3-excitatory-arrow)" />
            <path class="connection supporting" d="M 187 95 L 146 46" marker-end="url(#ca3-excitatory-arrow)" />
            <path class="connection inhibitory supporting" d="M 110 27 Q 40 34 51 84" marker-end="url(#ca3-inhibitory-bar)" />
            <path class="connection inhibitory supporting" d="M 150 27 Q 220 34 209 84" marker-end="url(#ca3-inhibitory-bar)" />
            <path class="connection emphasized" d="M 80 103 L 176 103" marker-end="url(#ca3-excitatory-arrow)" />
            <path class="connection emphasized" d="M 180 119 L 84 119" marker-end="url(#ca3-excitatory-arrow)" />
            <circle class="interneuron" cx="130" cy="27" r="19" />
            <circle class="pyramidal" cx="60" cy="111" r="19" />
            <circle class="pyramidal" cx="200" cy="111" r="19" />
            <text class="cell-letter interneuron-letter" x="130" y="32">I</text>
            <text class="cell-letter" x="60" y="116">P</text>
            <text class="cell-letter" x="200" y="116">P</text>
          </svg>
          <p>Both cell types are present. Highlighted P–P connections amplify population activity and are absent in the model's CA1 network.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="local-circuit">
          <h3>CA1 · Recurrent inhibition</h3>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 260 140" role="img" aria-labelledby="ca1-circuit-title">
            <title id="ca1-circuit-title">Two PV interneurons with reciprocal inhibitory connections and a pyramidal neuron</title>
            <defs>
              <marker id="ca1-excitatory-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="10" refY="5" markerWidth="9" markerHeight="9" markerUnits="userSpaceOnUse" orient="auto">
                <path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" class="arrowhead" />
              </marker>
              <marker id="ca1-inhibitory-bar" viewBox="0 0 4 14" refX="2" refY="7" markerWidth="4" markerHeight="14" markerUnits="userSpaceOnUse" orient="auto">
                <rect x="0.75" y="1" width="2.5" height="12" class="inhibitory-head" />
              </marker>
            </defs>
            <path class="connection supporting" d="M 116 44 L 76 92" marker-end="url(#ca1-excitatory-arrow)" />
            <path class="connection supporting" d="M 144 44 L 184 92" marker-end="url(#ca1-excitatory-arrow)" />
            <path class="connection inhibitory supporting" d="M 51 91 Q 38 40 103 27" marker-end="url(#ca1-inhibitory-bar)" />
            <path class="connection inhibitory supporting" d="M 209 91 Q 222 40 157 27" marker-end="url(#ca1-inhibitory-bar)" />
            <path class="connection inhibitory emphasized" d="M 80 103 L 174 103" marker-end="url(#ca1-inhibitory-bar)" />
            <path class="connection inhibitory emphasized" d="M 180 119 L 86 119" marker-end="url(#ca1-inhibitory-bar)" />
            <circle class="pyramidal" cx="130" cy="27" r="19" />
            <circle class="interneuron" cx="60" cy="111" r="19" />
            <circle class="interneuron" cx="200" cy="111" r="19" />
            <text class="cell-letter" x="130" y="32">P</text>
            <text class="cell-letter interneuron-letter" x="60" y="116">I</text>
            <text class="cell-letter interneuron-letter" x="200" y="116">I</text>
          </svg>
          <p>Both cell types are present. Highlighted I–I connections help coordinate ripple activity and are absent in the model's CA3 network.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <NeuronModels />
      <div class="circuit-legend">
        <span><svg class="legend-icon" viewBox="0 0 20 16" aria-hidden="true"><circle class="pyramidal" cx="10" cy="8" r="4" /></svg>P · pyramidal cell</span>
        <span><svg class="legend-icon" viewBox="0 0 20 16" aria-hidden="true"><circle class="interneuron" cx="10" cy="8" r="4" /></svg>I · PV interneuron</span>
        <span><svg class="legend-icon" viewBox="0 0 20 16" aria-hidden="true"><path class="connection" d="M 2 8 H 12" /><path class="arrowhead" d="M 11 3.5 L 20 8 L 11 12.5 Z" /></svg>Excitation</span>
        <span><svg class="legend-icon" viewBox="0 0 20 16" aria-hidden="true"><path class="connection" d="M 2 8 H 16" /><rect class="inhibitory-head" x="14.75" y="2" width="2.5" height="12" /></svg>Inhibition</span>
        <span class="schematic-note">Simplified circuit motifs; not all connections are shown.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .model-architecture { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 112px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 28px; padding: 28px 0 var(--project-section-gap); border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .section-label { margin: 3px 0 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: var(--project-label-size); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .06em; }
  h2 { margin: 0; color: var(--text-strong); font-size: var(--project-heading-size); line-height: 1.3; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: -.01em; }
  .architecture-copy { max-width: 620px; margin: 14px 0 0; color: var(--text); font-size: var(--project-body-size); line-height: var(--project-body-leading); }
  .architecture-panel { margin: 22px 0 0; border: 1px solid var(--rule); background: #111310; }
  svg { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }
  .region-diagram { max-width: 600px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 18px 12px 0; }
  .region, .interneuron { fill: var(--background); stroke: var(--text-strong); stroke-width: 1.5; }
  .pyramidal, .arrowhead { fill: var(--text); }
  .connection { fill: none; stroke: var(--text); stroke-width: 1.5; }
  .supporting { opacity: .55; }
  .emphasized { stroke-width: 2.2; }
  .inhibitory { stroke-dasharray: 4 3; }
  .inhibitory-head { fill: var(--text); stroke: none; stroke-dasharray: none; }
  text { fill: var(--muted); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; text-anchor: middle; }
  .region-name { fill: var(--text-strong); font-size: 18px; }
  .diagram-note { font-size: 13px; }
  .local-circuits { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .local-circuit { min-width: 0; padding: 18px; }
  .local-circuit + .local-circuit { border-left: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  h3 { margin: 0; color: var(--text-strong); font-size: var(--project-body-size); line-height: 1.4; font-weight: 500; }
  .local-circuit svg { max-width: 260px; margin: 16px auto 12px; }
  .cell-letter { fill: var(--background); font-size: 14px; }
  .interneuron-letter { fill: var(--text-strong); }
  .local-circuit p { margin: 0; color: var(--text); font-size: var(--project-support-size); line-height: 1.6; }
  .circuit-legend { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 10px 18px; padding: 14px 18px; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); color: var(--muted); font-size: var(--project-support-size); line-height: 1.6; }
  .circuit-legend span { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; }
  .legend-icon { flex: 0 0 20px; width: 20px; height: 16px; }
  .schematic-note { flex-basis: 100%; color: var(--faint); }
  @media (max-width: 620px) {
    .model-architecture { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 12px; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 440px) {
    .local-circuits { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .local-circuit + .local-circuit { border-left: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
    .region-diagram { padding-right: 4px; padding-left: 4px; }
  }
</style>
